 "id": "2026-11-28-b",
 "title": "Australia lost a war to emus 🪶",
 "description": "In November 1932, emus were wrecking wheat farms in Western Australia's Campion district, so the army sent Major G. P. W. Meredith, two soldiers, two Lewis guns and 10,000 rounds. The emus split into small groups and scattered, a gun jammed, and a gun mounted on a truck couldn't catch them on rough ground. Meredith's own report: 986 emus for 9,860 rounds, exactly ten per bird. He said they could \"face machine guns with the invulnerability of tanks.\" The army withdrew in December 1932; bounties (about 57,000 claimed in six months of 1934) and long exclusion fences did the job instead.\n\nSources: Encyclopaedia Britannica, \"Emu War\"; Wikipedia, \"Emu War\"; History Hit, \"The Great Emu War\".",
